cover after Spaulding Rehabilitation  Hospital was hit by Hurricane Katrina in  2005  it took an innovative approach to  prepare for any future disasters that  might take place and made sure its  patients can be safe at all times in  2013 the city introduced a brand new  building that looks completely prepared  for climate change and hurricanes to  start it off the design of the building  makes  that all primary electrical services are  located on the rooftop to make sure the  building's electricity does not get  affected by the floods the electricity  itself is powered by a fuel pump which  is secured by a flood proof vault the  actual ground floor is elevated by 2.5  feet which protects the hospital from  any potential flooding even the outside  of the place has landscape walls which  act like a reef in the event of a storm  all of these precautions ensure that the  building can still function and the  patients can still be taken care of  during a natural disaster the building  looks pretty solid and definitely ready  to protect itself and its patients  during a hurricane seems like the  Spaulding Rehabilitation Hospital truly  is safe and ready for hurricanes this  ferry we often see the shocking  aftermath of cities being hit by a  high-level hurricane many of the  buildings end up completely destroyed or  flooded and the damage can cost the city  billions of dollars but sometimes  depending on the circumstances larger  ships and boats can survive natural  disasters when northern Japan was hit by  an a tsunami following an earthquake in  2011 it left one of the most devastating  damages on the seaside cities with many  buildings that ended up being destroyed  it's hard to believe that this ferry  remains completely undisturbed even  though it's positioned on top of the  building and clearly went through some  damage you can clearly see the table and  chairs on the deck being completely  intact boats are very much at nature's  mercy when coming in contact with strong  weather conditions but this ferry was  able to survive the damages of a strong  earthquake along with the tsunami  following afterward while many smaller  and weaker boats and ships aren't as  lucky when it comes to natural disasters  large ferries and cruise ships can  definitely survive a tsunami especially  if they're docked and tied with extra  strong materials while the strong waves  could potentially knock the ship against  the pier the ship structure would most  likely survive the Hurricanes impact of  course this also depends on the severity  of the tsunami as well as the position  of the ship itself Sir Richard Branson  although he's definitely not  indestructible like some of the houses  and other buildings were mentioning in  this video it's worthy to mention how  the business tycoon survived the 2017  hurricane Irma as it made its way across  the Caribbean and Florida at the time of  the hurricane Sir Richard Branson  located on his private island in the  Caribbean despite knowing that the  hurricane will directly impact the  island and the surrounding area the  businessman decided to stay put with his  family knowing they will most likely  stay unharmed there the family spent the  night in their wine cellar where they  experienced a night of howling wind and  rain although he considered this to be a  fun sleepover it's safe to say that the  somewhat indestructible Sir Richard  Branson could face a different fate had  it not been for the sturdy wine cellar  which in his words would be running out  of wine by the time the storm would  subside although the rest of his private  island was pretty much destroyed by the  hurricane the wine cellar remained  intact it's important to note that this  is not always the case when it comes to  wine cellars as they could be the  victims of potential flooding with no  escape Sir Richard Branson might be an  indestructible business tycoon but we  have to admit he was pretty lucky in  this situation this standalone house no  this is not a photo shop but we can  assume that these houses got extremely  lucky when it came to avoiding potential  hurricane disasters one such was this  lucky house that survived the rage of  the 2008 Hurricane Ike which destroyed a  large portion of Southeast Texas and  caused 37.6 billion dollars worth of  damage  soon after the incredible images of the  last house standing went viral the house  is seen built at a higher level but  there is a good reason behind it the  people who lived here have already faced  a natural disaster that costs them their  previous home the owners of the house  Warren and Pam Adams previously lost a  home on the same lot to the 2005  Hurricane Rita the home was then  completely rebuilt but nothing could  prepare them for the destructive forces  of Hurricane Ike just three years later  while their home along with a couple of  other ones looked completely intact and  unaffected by the hurricane  the couple reported that it's not  inhabitable as the flood damaged most of  the rooms along with the appliances even  though the house was built 22 feet above  the normal sea level the flood still  managed to completely destroy the  interior but although the hurricane  damaged the interior of the house it is  still extraordinary that the exterior  remained completely intact and that's it  for ten things hurricanes cannot destroy  for more videos like this one check out  15 random acts of vandalism that are  your genius see you next time  [Music]

